# 基本文章編集: the desktop's own and the process write the same record and show the same
# page (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py. Two copies of 基本文章編集 with 30 paragraphs
# (mkbig doc 30) are given the same changes, one in the desktop's text editor (open) and one
# in the text editor running as a process (pdoc): the caret put in the second paragraph,
# abc typed (in the width the input mode says), one letter taken back with Backspace, a new
# paragraph with Enter, letters picked by carrying the hand across the fourth line and thrown
# away with Delete, then saved. Record 0 of both must be the same, byte for byte; the shots
# (doc_cmp_k_*, doc_cmp_p_*) are compared afterwards inside the window, where the text is
# (101,125 to 682,482 of the screen: the window stands at 100,100, 600 by 400). The pointer
# is put on the corner of the bars before the first shot of each.
# Keys: Backspace 2A, Enter 28, Delete 4C; Ctrl+S 16 01, Ctrl+E 08 01.
# the desktop's text editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (docproc kernel)
docproc kernel
mkbig doc 30
open big
waitwin 基本文章編集 600
sync 600
wait 500
move 690 490
sync 600
shot doc_cmp_k_open
click 300 170
sync 600
text abc
sync 600
key 2A
sync 600
key 28
sync 600
shot doc_cmp_k_typed
drag 160 230 420 230
sync 600
key 4C
sync 600
shot doc_cmp_k_done
key 16 01
sync 600
sum show
keep kernel
key 08 01
sync 600
wait 500
mkbig doc 30
logmark
pdoc big
expectsincein 60 document: opened 基本文章編集 paragraphs 30
wait 800
move 690 490
wait 300
shot doc_cmp_p_open
logmark
click 300 170
expectsince document: drew
logmark
text abc
expectsince document: key to screen
wait 300
logmark
key 2A
expectsince document: key to screen
logmark
key 28
expectsince document: key to screen
shot doc_cmp_p_typed
logmark
drag 160 230 420 230
expectsince document: drew
logmark
key 4C
expectsince document: key to screen
shot doc_cmp_p_done
logmark
key 16 01
expectsince document: saved (0)
sum show
same kernel
key 08 01
expect document: closed
